Subject: [PATCH] Analysis framework planned before fieldwork (research
 intelligence, Phase 2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What each question is FOR, and what the study will run, now live in the
definition and are read and written by the copilot, the Studio and the
engine alike:

- question.analysis: role (dependent / independent / mediator / moderator /
  control / segmentation / screening / descriptive), measurement level,
  how it is reported, what it is tabulated against, what it relates to,
  modelling, construct, hypotheses (H1, H2…). Inferred by the engine from
  the type, the research design and the question's place; the Studio shows
  the inference as such and stores only what is set.
- research.analysisPlan: crosstabs (priority, hypotheses), tests (method,
  outcome, predictors, grouping, moderator, mediator), derived variables,
  segments. buildAnalysisFramework proposes one from roles and levels:
  outcomes by the banner, nominal IV × DV tables, correlation / regression
  (moderation, mediation), t-test / ANOVA / chi-square by level, MaxDiff /
  conjoint / NPS, reliability and mean scores for multi-item constructs.
- Hypothesis coverage (testable / partly / unmeasured / unlinked);
  prioritised crosstabs ("the most important first"); methodologyAdvice
  (goal → recommended method and trade-offs).
- Impact: deleting a question lists what the plan loses and prunes the
  plan; renaming a variable follows it; the review reports a plan that no
  longer fits (dead references, wrong test for the level or group count).
- Actions: set_question_analysis, propose_analysis_plan, set_analysis_plan,
  add/remove_crosstab, add/remove_analysis_test, add/remove_derived_variable
  — gated, every variable resolved, unknown methods refused by name; the
  ANALYSIS GUIDE and the plan (with ids) go to the model on analysis turns
  and generation; the diff summary names the plan's changes; the card shows
  the gate's refusal reasons.
- Studio: Properties → Analysis per question; Intelligent → Analysis tab
  (hypotheses, checks, crosstabs, tests, variables, plan / merge / re-plan,
  confirmed removal, methodology advice).
- Analytics: plannedAnalyses turns the plan into AnalysisDefinitions in the
  runners' order; POST analyses/from-plan and "Create the planned analyses"
  create them once responses exist, hypothesis-linked first, never twice.

Tests: engine analysisFramework (9, 43/43 mutations caught), analytics
planBridge (3, 10/10), studio copilot (+1), browser analysis-framework (7,
9/9 Studio mutations caught). docs/ANALYSIS-FRAMEWORK-2026-10-04.md.

